HtmlViewer.tsx confirms what I suspected. I’ve patched it, and the ⛶ button should now go fullscreen inside the widget. I haven’t built or run it.

What was blocking the button

1. The <iframe> had no allow="fullscreen", so requestFullscreen() was always rejected.

2. The sandbox had allow-popups but not allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox. The new-tab fallback would have opened a tab that was itself sandboxed.


1. It adds allow="fullscreen" and allowFullScreen to the iframe.
2. It adds a local HTML_WIDGET_SANDBOX_ATTRIBUTES, which is the 
shared constant plus allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox. I left constants.ts 
alone so the other iframe widgets and plugin frames keep their sandbox.


